    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300-a2">

                <pb facs="0616" n="492" xml:id="pg492"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    254.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Dr. Busch to Mr.
                            Everett</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1881-09-24"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 24,
                    1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, referring to the note from the foreign office of the 21st
                    instant, has the honor to inform Mr. H. Sidney Everett, chargé d’affaires <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ad interim</hi> of the United States of America, that
                    another member of the von Steuben family of Falkenberg, will have the honor to
                    accept the invitation of the President and people of the United States to take
                    part in the centennial celebration of the capitulation of Yorktown, on the 19th
                    October next.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails himself of this occasion, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>BUSCH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
